n AD","nucleus_padj":0.7234,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0171899,"nucleus_score":-0.458478,"pct_ad":0.185701,"pct_control":0.188594,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.94266,"donor_log2fc":-0.0287347,"donor_lfcse":0.0746649,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00802354,"degas_log2fc":0.0845547,"degas_padj":0.151111},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"PLEKHM1","gene_symbol_current":"PLEKHM1","gene_id":"ENSG00000225190","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.86152,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.00944079,"nucleus_score":-0.278769,"pct_ad":0.170146,"pct_control":0.171719,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0144339,"donor_lfcse":0.104107,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-1.35033e-06,"degas_log2fc":-0.161966,"degas_padj":0.021924},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"PLEKHM1","gene_symbol_current":"PLEKHM1","gene_id":"ENSG00000225190","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.686463,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.000280689,"nucleus_score":-0.460186,"pct_ad":0.199775,"pct_control":0.201023,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.918654,"donor_log2fc":0.0707343,"donor_lfcse":0.107574,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00617184,"degas_log2fc":-0.119047,"degas_padj":6.84104e-06}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000225190","module":"blue","kme":0.0985751,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000225190","module":"blue","kme":0.104918,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000225190","entrez_id":["9842"],"uniprot":["Q9Y4G2"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is essential for bone resorption, and may play a critical role in vesicular transport in the osteoclast. Mutations in this gene are associated with autosomal recessive osteopetrosis type 6 (OPTB6). Alternatively spliced transcript variants have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Sep 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y4G2","text":"Acts as a multivalent adapter protein that regulates Rab7-dependent and HOPS complex-dependent fusion events in the endolysosomal system and couples autophagic and the endocytic trafficking pathways. Acts as a dual effector of RAB7A and ARL8B that simultaneously binds these GTPases, bringing about clustering and fusion of late endosomes and lysosomes (PubMed:25498145, PubMed:28325809). Required for late stages of endolysosomal maturation, facilitating both endocytosis-mediated degradation of growth factor receptors and autophagosome clearance. Interaction with Arl8b is a crucial factor in the terminal maturation of autophagosomes and to mediate autophagosome-lysosome fusion (PubMed:25498145). Positively regulates lysosome peripheral distribution and ruffled border formation in osteoclasts (By similarity). May be involved in negative regulation of endocytic transport from early endosome to late endosome/lysosome implicating its association with Rab7 (PubMed:20943950). May have a role in sialyl-lex-mediated transduction of apoptotic signals (PubMed:12820725). Involved in bone resorption (By similarity). (Microbial infection) In case of infection contributes to Salmonella typhimurium pathogenesis by supporting the integrity of the Salmonella-containing vacuole (SCV) probably in concert with the HOPS complex and Rab7."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}